{"nodes": [{"id": "progress_decisions_review_doc_client_work_order", "label": "Client Review and Standing Work Order", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "progress/decisions/Review Doc.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The client's response to the Week 3 summary: direction call, fold fix, reporting standards and the rest of the work order."}, {"id": "progress_decisions_review_doc_hold_five_seeds", "label": "Hold the Five Seeds Until the Folds Are Fixed", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "progress/decisions/Review Doc.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Three of four datasets are influenza, so holding out flu-Japan still leaves flu-US-regions and flu-US-states in training; spending five seeds on the wrong fold structure buys nothing because the compute is gone and the paper still lacks its number."}, {"id": "progress_decisions_review_doc_leave_one_disease_out_fold", "label": "Leave-One-Disease-Out Fold", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "progress/decisions/Review Doc.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "All three influenza datasets held out together as one fold with dengue as the other; the honest cross-disease number the central claim rests on, expected to come in weaker than the current headline."}, {"id": "progress_decisions_review_doc_leave_one_dataset_out_fold", "label": "Leave-One-Dataset-Out Fold", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "progress/decisions/Review Doc.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Kept as a real result about population transfer and reported as a separate table beside the disease-level fold."}, {"id": "progress_decisions_review_doc_reporting_standards", "label": "Reporting Standards Effective Immediately", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "progress/decisions/Review Doc.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Dispersion on every number, bootstrap CIs over regions and origins for headlines, never average across datasets, state the comparison reference on the table, and write within noise rather than a direction below the noise floor."}, {"id": "progress_decisions_review_doc_meta_learning_required", "label": "Meta-Learning Is Required, Not Optional", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "progress/decisions/Review Doc.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "What is implemented is transfer learning with a linear probe; the brief marks meta-learning REQUIRED under G2 and the encoder was chosen for cheap second-order differentiation, an argument that only pays off if it is used. Freeze-and-adapt becomes the ablation."}, {"id": "progress_decisions_review_doc_ebola_audit_request", "label": "Ebola Audit Request", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "progress/decisions/Review Doc.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The biggest open risk: resolution, usable origins, missingness across 61 units, adjacency, and how many labelled support examples exist. If Ebola comes in under the 27-example few-shot design floor the constraint was calibrated against the wrong thing."}, {"id": "progress_decisions_review_doc_baseline_head_to_head", "label": "Baseline Head-to-Head Gate", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "progress/decisions/Review Doc.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Every locked-shortlist baseline on the common pipeline, all four datasets and horizons, each validated against its source paper's published numbers before it may enter the comparison table."}, {"id": "progress_decisions_review_doc_reproduction_failure_log", "label": "Reproduction Failure Log", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "progress/decisions/Review Doc.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Publishable on its own and far easier to keep as you go than to reconstruct at the end; combined with pre-registration it gives a credibility story most submissions in this space cannot tell."}, {"id": "progress_decisions_review_doc_metric_set_wis_crps", "label": "Required Metric Set (WIS, CRPS, Coverage, PIT, Peak, Scale-Normalised)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "progress/decisions/Review Doc.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "RMSE, MAE and PCC will not satisfy epidemic-forecasting reviewers and the project claims calibrated uncertainty; scale-normalised error is needed because across 7,165 dengue regions raw RMSE is dominated by the biggest ones."}, {"id": "progress_decisions_review_doc_conformal_split_reservation", "label": "Reserve the Conformal Calibration Split Now", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "progress/decisions/Review Doc.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Vanilla split conformal assumes exchangeability and the setup breaks it on two axes at once, temporal dependence and shift onto an unseen disease; a shift and time aware variant must be picked before the Ebola work because retrofitting the split is painful."}, {"id": "progress_decisions_review_doc_explainability_scoping", "label": "Explainability Scoping Note", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "progress/decisions/Review Doc.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "SHAP over a spatio-temporal GNN with 7,165 regions is a serious compute proposition and with four input channels it is not obvious what is being attributed over; integrated gradients is probably more tractable."}, {"id": "progress_decisions_review_doc_preregistration_score_once", "label": "Pre-Registration and Scoring Ebola Once", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "progress/decisions/Review Doc.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Adopted as a stated methodological contribution rather than an internal process note: cheap, unusual in this literature, and a credibility story when paired with the failure log."}, {"id": "progress_decisions_review_doc_deprioritise_t52_lag", "label": "Do Not Add a t-52 Lag Channel", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "progress/decisions/Review Doc.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "It would fix the benchmark row, but Ebola has no prior year so the channel would be permanently null for the actual target: a train and target mismatch introduced to win a table cell."}, {"id": "progress_decisions_review_doc_covid_third_disease", "label": "Add COVID-19 Back as a Third Development Disease", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "progress/decisions/Review Doc.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Restructured folds make the claim honest and a third disease makes it strong."}, {"id": "progress_decisions_review_doc_joint_sampler_remedies", "label": "Try the Obvious Joint-Training Remedies Before Declaring Failure", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "progress/decisions/Review Doc.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Dengue is about 98% of training examples, so a reviewer will ask whether the sampler was balanced; if balanced or temperature-scaled sampling, per-disease loss reweighting and per-dataset normalisation still fail, the negative result stops reading as an unfinished experiment."}, {"id": "progress_decisions_review_doc_arima_gbm_baselines", "label": "Add ARIMA/SARIMA and a Gradient-Boosted Lag Model", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "progress/decisions/Review Doc.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The GBM in particular is hard to beat and it is better to find that out internally than from a reviewer."}, {"id": "progress_decisions_review_doc_graph_gate_figure", "label": "Build the Learned Graph Gate Figure", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "progress/decisions/Review Doc.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Gate values of 0.27 to 0.60 scaling with region count and density is already an interpretable result and is being under-used."}], "edges": [{"source": "progress_decisions_review_doc_client_work_order", "target": "progress_decisions_review_doc_hold_five_seeds", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "progress/decisions/Review Doc.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "progress_decisions_review_doc_client_work_order", "target": "progress_decisions_review_doc_reporting_standards", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "progress/decisions/Review Doc.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "progress_decisions_review_doc_client_work_order", "target": "progress_decisions_review_doc_meta_learning_required", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "progress/decisions/Review Doc.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "progress_decisions_review_doc_client_work_order", "targ